    <header class="mb-12"><p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.25em] font-mono text-accent mb-4">SecureByteGuide · Trust</p><h1 class="text-5xl md:text-6xl font-bold leading-[0.95] mb-4" style="font-family:var(--font-display);">Terms of Use</h1><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Last updated: September 6, 2026</p></header>
    <div class="prose-article space-y-8 text-[16px] leading-[1.75]">
<section><h2>Acceptance and permitted use</h2><p>By using SecureByteGuide, you agree to these terms. You may read, link to, and quote limited portions of the site with attribution for lawful personal, educational, or editorial use. Do not disrupt the service, bypass security controls, scrape it abusively, impersonate the publication, or use the site to facilitate unlawful access or harm.</p></section>
<section><h2>Informational scope</h2><p>Articles and tools provide general digital-safety information, not legal, financial, forensic, emergency, or individualized professional advice. Technology, threats, provider rules, and laws change. Check current official instructions and seek qualified help when the situation involves active compromise, money movement, regulated data, workplace systems, physical safety, or legal duties.</p></section>
